    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\n`require('vim._core.mcursor').number()` (`g CTRL-A` helper) throws\n`E5108: 'replacement string' item contains newlines` when `format`\ncontains `\\n`.\n\nRelated code `runtime/lua/vim/_core/mcursor.lua:247`:\n```lua\nvim.api.nvim_buf_set_text(0, p.row, p.col, p.row, p.col, { format:format(...) })\n```\n\n`nvim_buf_set_text` expects string[] with one line per element; a single\nstring with embedded \\n is rejected. The C preview path\n`src/nvim/mcursor.c:741` `mc_ins_preview_replace` splits on \\n correctly,\nthis Lua path does not.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```lua\nvim.api.nvim_buf_set_lines(0,0,-1,true,{'x','x','x'})\nvim.api.nvim_mcursor(0,{2,0})\nvim.api.nvim_mcursor(0,{3,0})\nrequire('vim._core.mcursor').number(1,1,'%d\\n')\n```\n```sh\nE5108: Lua: vim/_core/mcursor:247: 'replacement string' item contains newlines\nstack traceback:\n  [C]: in function 'nvim_buf_set_text'\n  vim/_core/mcursor:247: in function 'number'\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nInserts numbers as multiline text bottom-up (existing logic already iterates\n#pts..1 to avoid shifting):\n{'1','x','2','x','3','x'} (6 lines) or documented error with vim.notify.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-739a447\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nNo, Vim has no multicursor\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nLinux Arch 7.2.2-arch1-1\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nKitty\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-kitty\n\n### Installation\n\nbuild from repo",
