        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> [@echasnovski](https://github.com/echasnovski) Not by default via `g CTRL-A` alone (`format=\"%d\"`). Only via Lua `number(..., '%d\\n')` / mapped `g<C-A>` not normal typing, but a plugin could pass `\\n` in `format`. Fix is just one `vim.split` before `nvim_buf_set_text` (like `mcursor.c:741`), so worth guarding.\n\nPlugins are encouraged to *not* use private functions. As long they are not exported, there are no guarantees about how they behave, what arguments they take, or even if they exist. So 1) I'd suggest to not use `require('vim._core.mcursor').number`; but even then 2) guard against such usages by not allowing `\\n` character in a replacement.\n\nEven fix might be easy, it is technically not needed with the currently exported set of functionality.",
            "created_at": "2026-09-05T17:01:47Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/41715#issuecomment-5553376279",
